## Setup & Installation

### Requirements

- [Homebrew](https://brew.sh) and [go-task](https://taskfile.dev)
[% if use_node %]
- Node >= 22 and [pnpm](https://pnpm.io)
[% endif %]
[% if use_python %]
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (Python is pinned in `.python-version`)
[% endif %]

### Install

```bash
task bootstrap   # one-time machine setup (Homebrew[% if use_node %] + Node + pnpm[% endif %])
task install     # Brewfile deps[% if use_python %] + uv sync[% endif %][% if use_node %] + pnpm install[% endif %] + lefthook git hooks
task verify      # confirm everything passes
```

Or open the repo in the devcontainer (VS Code "Reopen in Container", or a
[Coder](https://coder.com) workspace)[% if devcontainer %] — the human profile lives in
`.devcontainer/dev/`, the AI/bot profile at `.devcontainer/`[% endif %].

New here? Start with [docs/guides/onboarding.md](docs/guides/onboarding.md) and the
post-generation [docs/CHECKLIST.md](docs/CHECKLIST.md).
[% if project_type in ['web-astro', 'web-app'] %]

### Web app scaffolding

This template ships shared conventions (lint, hooks, CI, docs) — not the web app
itself. Scaffold the app with the framework's own tool first, then re-apply the
template to overlay conventions:

```bash
[% if project_type == 'web-astro' %]
pnpm create astro@latest .             # scaffold the Astro site in-place
[% else %]
pnpm create @tanstack/router@latest    # scaffold the TanStack + React app
[% endif %]
copier update --trust                  # overlay/refresh harmon-init conventions
```

See [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) for visual/UX direction.
[% endif %]

